# Build context for every image built from the repository root (F-002-T14; SEC-F002-29).
# The build stage copies the context, so anything listed here can never be baked into an image
# layer, whatever a Dockerfile's COPY says. `secret-scan-cli.ts image` scans the result anyway.

# Credentials and anything that could hold one: generated dev-stack files (deploy/docker/dev/.env
# holds the Postgres password and the OpenBao root token), every .env, keys and certificates.
**/.env
**/.env.*
deploy/docker/dev/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.kdbx
**/.npmrc
**/.netrc

# Version control, CI, local tools and agent worktrees.
.git
.github
.githooks
.claude
.tools
.idea
.vscode

# Installs and build output: the image installs and builds from the lockfile itself.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.tsc
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.audit-spool
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Content that no image build reads.
docs
requirements
packs
